[d7e72fcada30b181] (mini.proposal.v1)
I propose testing the 'conformance.kernel.response-verdict' kernel with the 'conformance.transform.prose-after' transform. The catalogue shows that adding prose before a JSON object (conformance.transform.prose-before) does not move the response verdict (it remains JSON_OBJECT), as the harness successfully recovers the object. However, adding prose after the object (conformance.transform.prose-after) makes the reply no longer strict JSON. While the recovery kernel might still find the object, I expect the response verdict to move from JSON_OBJECT to something else (like INVALID_JSON or a recovery-based verdict) because the overall reply is no longer a bare JSON object.
commitments: {"kernel": "conformance.kernel.response-verdict", "transform": "conformance.transform.prose-after", "input": "{\"claimant_name\": \"amara okoro\", \"total_days\": \"five\"}"}

